    <bpmn:process id="W_W1628" name="W1628. Customer Return Trend Analysis &amp; Fraud Detection" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly returns analysis cycle or real-time fraud alert
Frequency: Monthly trend analysis; real-time fraud monitoring
Volume: ~56,000 returns/month across 200 stores
Owner: Loss Prevention Manager
Participants: Loss Prevention Manager, Store Managers, Customer Service Manager, Finance
Source: workflow W1628 — Customer Return Trend Analysis &amp; Fraud Detection</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1628_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1628_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1628_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1628_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1628_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1628_Lane2" name="Loss Prevention Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1628_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1628_Lane3" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1628_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1628_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1628_Start5" name="Monthly returns analysis cycle or real-time fraud alert">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1628_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1628_Task6" name="System continuously monitors return patterns for fraud indicators: (a) same…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System continuously monitors return patterns for fraud indicators: (a) same customer &gt; 5 returns in 30 days, (b) no-receipt returns &gt; 3 per customer in 6 months, (c) returns of high-value items without original packaging, (d) return rate by store &gt; 3% (flag vs. chain average ~2%), (e) returns processed by same CSR with high frequency (&gt; 20% of store returns), (f) price difference between original purchase and return credit (switch fraud — buy on sale, return at full price using old receipt)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Loss Prevention Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1628_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1628_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1628_Task7" name="Real-time alerts: system sends fraud alert to Loss Prevention Manager and Store…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Real-time alerts: system sends fraud alert to Loss Prevention Manager and Store Manager for flagged transactions; Store Manager has authority to deny return if fraud suspected
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1628_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1628_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1628_Task8" name="Monthly: Loss Prevention Manager generates Returns Analytics Report: (a) return…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly: Loss Prevention Manager generates Returns Analytics Report: (a) return rate by store, by category, by reason code, (b) return rate trend (monthly, quarterly, YoY), (c) top 20 items by return volume, (d) top 20 customers by return frequency, (e) return fraud cases detected and resolved, (f) financial impact of returns (revenue reversal, handling cost, markdown cost)
Responsible (R): Loss Prevention Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1628_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1628_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1628_Task9" name="Monthly: Category Manager reviews top 20 items by return volume; identifies…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly: Category Manager reviews top 20 items by return volume; identifies root causes: (a) quality issue → vendor VCAR (W1610), (b) product description mismatch → update product information (W50), (c) sizing confusion → update labeling and store signage, (d) packaging damage → improve packaging or handling procedure
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1628_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1628_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1628_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1628_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1628_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-179 (ensure returns integrity &amp; refund-fraud prevention.) | - operational: Loss Prevention Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Loss Prevention Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
